Function calls itself to solve smaller versions of the same problem.
Function calls itself within its own definition.
Two parts of Recursion: 
1. Base case - Stop condition (when to stop calling itself)
2. Recursive Case - part where function calls itself

Real life example:
1. If a person in queue has to find out how many are in queue, he will ask next to him
the same question and this continues and replies back to each will be the total number
in queue
2. comment threads
3. organisational hierarchies
ceo -> cto and cmo -> directors -> vps etc........
(how many work under you)

