Note:
code written before the recursive case will execute upgoing, code written after the 
recursive case will execute downgoing.(callstack - upgoing, downgoing(comingback))

Base case determines when recursion will stop.
Most of the time we write base case at top of the function.
 
. Infinite recursion leads to stack overflow.

